title op3: a severed directory moved under a different parent decays

# The one shape Section 16 gives up, asserted so that giving it up
# stays a decision rather than a surprise.
#
# Off-of moves box out of /src and into /dst, rebuilding it rather
# than renaming: the directory and its file both get fresh dnodes.
# The LEAF is unchanged -- it is box before and box after -- and the
# file's bytes are unchanged too.  Onto is quiet.
#
# A person reads this instantly.  Section 16 does not, and the reason
# is precise.  Candidates come from two generators.  The red anchor is
# dead, because nothing under the new box kept a dnode.  The sibling
# generator works INSIDE a corresponded pair, and box left its pair:
# under (/src, /src) there is a deletion and no addition, under
# (/dst, /dst) an addition and no deletion, and neither half can see
# the other.  So (base /src/box, off-of /dst/box) is never nominated,
# and what is never nominated is never judged.
#
# Yellow would have found it.  The file's bytes sit in both trees, so
# under the first draft of Definition 16.3 its yellow anchor would
# have nominated /dst/box and the move would have been believed.  The
# kernel lane removed yellow as a generator, because a nomination is
# the inverted question -- what, anywhere, is yellow to this child --
# and answering it needs a content index over the whole tree that the
# lazy pairwise oracle is designed not to be.  The theory names this
# exact shape as the price.
#
# It is worth being clear about what the price IS.  Not correctness:
# the decay is death plus birth, which is what happens today and what
# happened before Section 16.  The price is that a directory identity
# is not carried across, so the new box is a fresh dnode.  A cheaper
# generator that could see across corresponded pairs would recover
# it; none is proposed, and the shape is asserted here so that the
# day someone proposes one, the fixture is already written.
#
# Note the failure MODE, because it is not the one the other blocked
# fixtures show.  op3-emigrant and op3-nested-recreated have
# candidates and refuse them.  Here there is nothing to refuse.  A
# diagnostic that counts blocked beliefs would report zero for this
# tree and be telling the truth.
#
# WORKED OUTCOME (by hand, before any implementation ran)
#   believed moves:  none, and NO CANDIDATE was ever nominated for
#                    /src/box -- an unnominated belief, not a blocked
#                    one
#   deltas:          none; no pool changes its name set relative to
#                    any corresponded pair
#   decisions:       /src/box and its f die; /dst/box and its f are
#                    born; /src survives, empty
#   conflicts:       none, onto is quiet
#   emission:        unlink f then unlink box (children first), and
#                    link box then link f under /dst (parent first)

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: src/
      3-100: box/
        4-100: f = fv0
    5-100: dst/
      6-100: .keep = kv0

tree onto
  1-1: /
    2-100: src/
      3-100: box/
        4-100: f = fv0
    5-100: dst/
      6-100: .keep = kv0

tree offof
  1-1: /
    2-100: src/
    5-100: dst/
      6-100: .keep = kv0
      10-300: box/
        11-300: f = fv0

# --- expected result, worked by hand 2026-08-31 ---
expect clean

tree expected
  1-1: /
    5-100: dst
      6-100: .keep = kv0
      10-300: box
        11-300: f = fv0
    2-100: src/
